<Project>

    <PropertyGroup>
        <!-- The graph is watched, not only recorded. NuGet checks the restored graph
             against the advisory database and NU1901 to NU1904 are raised to errors, so
             a known-vulnerable package fails the restore. Left as warnings they would be
             true and green, printed into a log nobody reads.

             This repository is assembly with two .NET projects under tests/, and it had
             a lockfile and no audit. Eleven boards of this fleet were in that state on
             2026-08-18; jellyfin-plugin-watchlist was the twelfth, and switching this on
             there found a critical advisory that Scorecard had never reported.

             Mode all rather than direct, because both of those arrived as transitive
             packages that no project file referenced.

             Nothing is pinned here. Measured with the audit forced on from the command
             line, both projects report no advisory today. This is the detector.

             An XML comment may not contain two hyphens in a row, which is why the flags
             are named in prose. A draft elsewhere in this fleet spelled one out, left the
             file malformed, and the build failed on a property defined further down. -->
        <NuGetAudit>true</NuGetAudit>
        <NuGetAuditMode>all</NuGetAuditMode>
        <NuGetAuditLevel>low</NuGetAuditLevel>
        <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);NU1901;NU1902;NU1903;NU1904</WarningsAsErrors>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <PropertyGroup>
        <!-- A committed lockfile per project. Swarm.Tests had one and said so in its own
             project file; Swarm.Bench had neither, so two runs of the same commit could
             benchmark different code and neither would say so.

             It sits here rather than in the two project files precisely because of that:
             a project added under tests/ later is locked from its first restore instead
             of from the day somebody notices it is not. -->
        <RestorePackagesWithLockFile>true</RestorePackagesWithLockFile>
    </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
